{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies","id":1049457,"title":"Gangrel feeding Strategies.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-15T13:49:08-08:00","id":1049457,"title":"Gangrel feeding Strategies.","content":"was just thinking<br /> <br /> The Mekhet Can use auspex to find weakness, and obfuscated to hide themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nosferatu can cloak themselves with obfuscate too... and paralyze someone with fear.<br /> Ventrue can give commands with a reasonable certainty of being obeyed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Daeva can charm their way into getting what they want<br /> <br /> Hows a Gangrel get blood without either &quot;Causing a scene&quot; or learning other clans disciplines.<br /> <br /> Protean only becomes that useful for feeding at 5 dots. (turning into vapor, is an EXCELLENT way of bypassing locks) <br /> <br /> Well yes, they could just take a dot or 2 of herd or feeding ground.<br /> <br /> ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:03:30-08:00","id":1049467,"title":"","content":"Animalism. At lower BP, use Animalism to summon or control animals to feed on. At higher BP, create a blood orgy.<br /> <br /> I guess that's causing a scene, but Majesty is pretty dramatic too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:06:06-08:00","id":1049470,"title":"","content":"Protean 2 you can wall climbing and enter in an open window at fifth floor or slip inside the door fissure. <br /> With animalism you can eat animals until blood potency 3 or command the dog of a passer-by to run away in that isolated alleyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-15-2017, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:11:34-08:00","id":1049475,"title":"","content":"You can use 360 degree vision to check if nobody is looking, you can hunt as a dog, dingo, wolf etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:19:05-08:00","id":1049480,"title":"","content":"Haven of Soil in a place where blood is likely to run, traveling somewhere there's no competition for food, hitting her with the seductive beast or just being good at the fundamentals of hunting so you don't need any shortcuts. Bloodlines of course allow extra disciplines but you already touched on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:35:40-08:00","id":1049500,"title":"","content":"Making a scene isn't an issue in some places. Go after campers and night fishermen, coast guard or junkies. There's plenty of places no one's going to call the police or run to assist if they start hearing screaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:43:15-08:00","id":1049504,"title":"","content":"Drinking from an homeless, lonely drug-dealer, going in the slum and bite someone; the kiss is subtle and let your victim confused and not aware of the real nature of the kiss, she will not scream. Let him unconscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:34:14-08:00","id":1049530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1049470#post1049470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With animalism you can...command the dog of a passer-by to run away in that isolated alleyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey that's really clever! Less of a scene causer than the blood orgy.<br /> <br /> I always find Animalism to be the most underrated discipline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:14:05-08:00","id":1049548,"title":"","content":"Lashing out against prospective human prey for anonymous one night stands or aggravated assault against an isolated target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T22:57:51-08:00","id":1049709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1049530#post1049530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey that's really clever! Less of a scene causer than the blood orgy.<br /> <br /> I always find Animalism to be the most underrated discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Animalism is really powerful. The first let you command a flock of birds or a rat spy. The third let you summom every animal in a long range; even in city you can summon a biblic plague made of rats, birds, dogs.... and the swarm tilt from demon is really awsome: 1\u00f74 damages at turn that bypass armor, -2 to any rolls, no way to disperse the swarm without area attacks like flamethrowers or explosives.... <br /> And this just for the fkocks part, having 4-5 dogs to fight against your target is a really dangerous plus...<br /> The forth allows you to create a little riot against your enemy, or let your enemy fall in frenzy against her allies.<br /> <br /> I think the flock could arrive in 2-3 turns... anyway you could wait for your animals army, merged with concrete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-16-2017, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T04:58:27-08:00","id":1049792,"title":"","content":"Protean 1 + grapple is a great ambush tactic. Lashing Out to seduce-fear-dom someone is pretty clever. Animalism for animal blood. Blood bond people. <br /> <br /> Remember, the thing about Gangrel is that they're animalistic. That means we're going to be pushing towards hunting like an animal. Remember the Gangrel clan blurb in the core book? &quot;The Ones You Can't Kill.&quot; That really should be &quot;The Ones You Can't Stop.&quot; They're the ones that hunt you down and you can't stop them from the hunt - their Protean adaptions let them go anywhere, find you anywhere, overcome any obsticle. They chase you down, wear you out, and then when you can't run anymore, they pounce. Look at the Chase rules - this is exactly where Gangrel excel at. Can't be tired, have a good Stamina score for Stamina+Athletics runs, thank you Resilience. Protean 2 has several adaptions to help out here as well. <br /> <br /> With the exception of Animalism and agg-claws, the Gangrel power set is generally based around survival. Outlasting the opponents. Very Resistant oriented. Generally, resistance is passive and/or reactive, so you need to swing things into that direction. Arrange situations where you can pull out that resistance and make it shine. Chasing down victims or ambushing them (patience and all that) is the key here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:40:22-08:00","id":1050031,"title":"","content":"Gangrel may lack the social and mental disciplines of other clans, but an urban hunter willing to spend a little vitae to get plenty more could, for example, use Protean to turn into a dog or cat\u2014since they are predatory animals, after all\u2014and you don't need to do this to hunt animal prey, either.<br /> <br /> Just wander the streets for a few hours, pausing now and then to look piteous and bedraggled, whimpering or miaowing for attention. Eventually some compassionate soul or street person is going to at least want to pet you and give you a drink of water or a bit of their sandwich. Sniff and nuzzle at your prey in 'gratitude', followed by a happy lick at their palm or wrist or (if you can leap into their lap or arms) their neck, followed by a careful bite (you do have fangs, after all) . . . with any luck they may wander away from you feeling a little lightheaded (and you a little warmer with their blood), but it could just be explained as a long tiring day mixed with the warm fuzzies from taking care of a poor stray . . . and, of course, if they decide to take you in, there's nothing saying you <i>have </i>to stick around, unless you really want to.<br /> <br /> (And, of course, should you run afoul of someone less savory and more violently inclined, what are they going to say once the tables turn? &quot;I tried to stab a dog in that alleyway to get my jollies and it nearly tore my ear off&quot;? They might not even have anything to say if you decide to remove one more imperfect predator from the world to fill your veins . . .)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T21:38:18-08:00","id":1053627,"title":"","content":"Jump somebody in an alley, take their wallet and it's just another violent crime. If you let them live the act of feeding, as Marcus already stated, leaves your prey confused about what just happened attributing all side effects to a bump on their head.<br /> It's boring and inelegant but why complicate things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T23:15:18-08:00","id":1053672,"title":"","content":"... And if you kill your victim, command a couple of dogs to shred him. Another attack by dogs gone wild","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T02:08:21-08:00","id":1053714,"title":"","content":"&quot;Another&quot;? Is that a thing that happens in other parts of the world? It'd be national news here in Sweden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T03:32:36-08:00","id":1053736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053714#post1053714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Another&quot;? Is that a thing that happens in other parts of the world? It'd be national news here in Sweden.</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on the part of the world. Apparently there are a few thousand deaths from animal attacks world wide. Which, to be fair, is roughly the chance of being struck by lightning (about one in a million), given the population of the world. <br /> <br /> Its really more of a perception issue than anything. Media can make animal attacks sound more common than they are, or more rare than they are. In the US, not only do we have large tracks of forested area where visitors act dumb around wild animals, but there are actually videos that people make of animal attacks that saturate people's conciousness, making the issue seem larger than it actually is. <br /> <br /> The animal-savaging corpse is actually not a bad idea, but not quite for the reasons Marcus posted. Its possible, during an autopsy, to tell if a wound is made post-mortem, especially with the tropes and Investigation rules we have. So, it won't really fool the forensics. However, it absolutely will obscure the cause of death, leaving people in the dark. And animals feeding on a corpse another human killed in the streets is something pretty common. Especially rats. Vampires are uniquely built so that they don't leave forensic evidence behind at scenes. They naturally avoid cameras, they don't secrete oils, making fingerprints very rare, any blood or saliva that leaves their body rapidly decays to the point of uselessness (unless we're talking a really young vampire). So, even if police peg a dead body savaged by animals as a murder victim, there's no evidence of &quot;vampire&quot; left, nor any hard evidence pointing to the vampire in question. At best, they'd get an eye witness, and witness memorie are notoriously unreliable. <br /> <br /> Of course, murder in Sweden is notoriously low. Less than 50 a year, if wikipedia is to believed; even lower if we make distinction between manslaughter and murder. Any local vampires are going to have to be very careful with feeding to avoid notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T03:33:48-08:00","id":1053737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053627#post1053627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's boring and inelegant but why complicate things.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps that's great neonate logic, but once you start hitting the ancillae and elder levels? Complicating things for the sake of holding off ennui is pretty much a given.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T05:25:33-08:00","id":1053764,"title":"","content":"Ghoul a small group of people, seriously, you have immortality without undeath to offer. <br /> <br /> Your pay for sex and apply the kiss during it. Just because your a Gangrel doesn't mean you always have to act like a thug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T05:26:38-08:00","id":1053765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053736#post1053736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Depends on the part of the world. Apparently there are a few thousand deaths from animal attacks world wide. Which, to be fair, is roughly the chance of being struck by lightning (about one in a million), given the population of the world. <br /> <br /> Its really more of a perception issue than anything. Media can make animal attacks sound more common than they are, or more rare than they are. In the US, not only do we have large tracks of forested area where visitors act dumb around wild animals, but there are actually videos that people make of animal attacks that saturate people's conciousness, making the issue seem larger than it actually is. <br /> <br /> The animal-savaging corpse is actually not a bad idea, but not quite for the reasons Marcus posted. Its possible, during an autopsy, to tell if a wound is made post-mortem, especially with the tropes and Investigation rules we have. So, it won't really fool the forensics. However, it absolutely will obscure the cause of death, leaving people in the dark. And animals feeding on a corpse another human killed in the streets is something pretty common. Especially rats. Vampires are uniquely built so that they don't leave forensic evidence behind at scenes. They naturally avoid cameras, they don't secrete oils, making fingerprints very rare, any blood or saliva that leaves their body rapidly decays to the point of uselessness (unless we're talking a really young vampire). So, even if police peg a dead body savaged by animals as a murder victim, there's no evidence of &amp;quot;vampire&amp;quot; left, nor any hard evidence pointing to the vampire in question. At best, they'd get an eye witness, and witness memorie are notoriously unreliable. <br /> <br /> Of course, murder in Sweden is notoriously low. Less than 50 a year, if wikipedia is to believed; even lower if we make distinction between manslaughter and murder. Any local vampires are going to have to be very careful with feeding to avoid notice.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is the CoD everywhere the murder rates are higher then in the RL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:41:48-08:00","id":1053923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053714#post1053714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Another&quot;? Is that a thing that happens in other parts of the world? It'd be national news here in Sweden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're right that nowadays in many parts of the World it would be in national news, but keep in mind that many ST choose XVIII or XIX century for the campaign. I guess that it used to be more accidents like that in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:54:39-08:00","id":1053928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053737#post1053737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps that's great neonate logic, but once you start hitting the ancillae and elder levels? Complicating things for the sake of holding off ennui is pretty much a given.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh this is so my favorite part of vampire. Vampires making conflict for themselves just because they're bored.<br /> <br /> EDIT: also known as: why the Carthian Movement, devoted to solutions, has very few Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","user":"RomulusGloriosus","date":".  follow up 02-23-2017, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:40:44-08:00","id":1053952,"title":"","content":"With all the problems Sweden has with migrants you'd just have to make sure your little accident happened in the right area and it may not make the news there either, especially if it was made to look as if it began as a rape and then escalated.<br /> In general, Gangrel seem to be well suited to violent and ambush feeding even if it's masked as a simple mugging or assault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:33:25-08:00","id":1053981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053765#post1053765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the CoD everywhere the murder rates are higher then in the RL.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. While that can be true for your game, that's not a good universal thing to assume. <br /> <br /> And, even if it was true, that doesn't change that Sweden has an insanely low murder rate, so that would still prompt more careful vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T15:32:59-08:00","id":1054048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053952#post1053952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all the problems Sweden has with migrants you'd just have to make sure your little accident happened in the right area and it may not make the news there either, especially if it was made to look as if it began as a rape and then escalated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our migrant problem is severely overstated. Rape-turned-murder would most likely make national headlines. And if it happened in any way that suggests that an immigrant did it our rightwing extremists would definitely use it to push their xenophobic agenda meaning everyone would soon know about it because people won't shut up about it.<br /> I'm seriously fucking tired of how Sweden is thought of by people who have zero insight into what's actually going on. I suggest anyone who wants an insider perspective or actual facts to read <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/petter.karlsson.92/posts/10210280710906410?pnref=story\" target=\"_blank\">this post</a> written by a friend of mine.<br /> <br /> I realise the world is definitely darker in CofD, but the reputation Sweden has gained has very little basis in reality. It's not the &quot;deeper shadows&quot; that the world of CofD says it portrays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T16:30:55-08:00","id":1054076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1053981#post1053981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nope. While that can be true for your game, that's not a good universal thing to assume.<br /> <br /> And, even if it was true, that doesn't change that Sweden has an insanely low murder rate, so that would still prompt more careful vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thank you. I was gonna say something but I figure that &quot;our world, but darker&quot; is such a deeply ingrained belief on WoD/CofD that I didn't see the point.<br /> <br /> Our world is already dark. Find the dark parts of your world, and focus on them. No need to change a thing. (Well except for the existence of vampires.....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T17:41:42-08:00","id":1054105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1049457-gangrel-feeding-strategies?p=1054048#post1054048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm seriously fucking tired of how Sweden is thought of by people who have zero insight into what's actually going on. I suggest anyone who wants an insider perspective or actual facts to read <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/petter.karlsson.92/posts/10210280710906410?pnref=story\" target=\"_blank\">this post</a> written by a friend of mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting to hear. It's tricky, because while we don't hear much about these things, when we do it's one side trying to push it into the media and they make it out like a nationwide epidemic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I realise the world is definitely darker in CofD, but the reputation Sweden has gained has very little basis in reality. It's not the &quot;deeper shadows&quot; that the world of CofD says it portrays. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, and at the risk of beating a dead horse, the darkness in Chronicles is mystery, not necessarily crime, and that mystery is not always linked to murder. World of Darkness touted a much higher crime rate and evil all around, but that stopped being an issue in Chronicles after the first Vampire the Requiem book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T05:37:40-08:00","id":1054275,"title":"","content":"*Shrugs* Its a classic World of Darkness thing. Corruption is / was more prevalent in that World. People try and carry things over from that World to the Chronicles all the time and assume its true. At this point, its just something you have to deal with. CofD is always going to live in the WoD's shadow, just like every high fantasy game is in D&amp;D's shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:42:43-08:00","id":1054418,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Sweden is not like Germany where the gov and media actively suppress news of migrant crimes, I've heard stories like that cop on facebook but I'm not familiar enough with Sweden to know for sure. It would be quite easy to fit into a VTR story though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 02-24-2017, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:49:31-08:00","id":1054450,"title":"","content":"Could I recommend that this isn't the subject for xenophobic conspiracy theories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T16:32:12-08:00","id":1054500,"title":"","content":"Sure, if I could recommend that this isn't the subject for childish name calling and ignorant dismissiveness of verifiable events?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 02-24-2017, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T17:30:27-08:00","id":1054526,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me. For the record, was not intending to call you personally xenophobic, but rather the argument. <br /> <br /> More on topic, not all feeding strategies have to involve disciplines. A Gangrel still has access to the Seductive predatory